text=['# GEMM and 2DCONV: matched F128 controls','', 'This packet consumes exactly eight closed accepted sources: original CH-P0/DH-P0/DH-F128 and authorized new CH-F128 for each frozen input. No F256 result is included, no new simulation was started, and no owner, controller, input, budget, source, manuscript or historical result was changed. Both new CH results were independently rechecked through the frozen read-only strict/archive/native-restore adapter. Seventy CPU-only evidence checks passed.','', 'GEMM is an exact zero-response control under the fixed replay initial-state policy. 2DCONV is a positive DH response with exact CH zero response: DH speedup 1.057515x (5.75% more throughput, 5.44% fewer simulated cycles). Neither finding establishes an equal-area hardware comparison.','', '## Exact identity and actual ROI','',table(['Program','Full input digest','Kernel symbol','Grid / block','Retired active-thread instructions','CTAs'],[[n,d['full_input_digest'],d['four_closed_sources'][0]['kernels'][0]['kernel'],str(next(x for x in W if x['program']==n)['bounded_header_grid'])+' / '+str(next(x for x in W if x['program']==n)['bounded_header_block']),json.loads((O/n/'INPUT_CONTRACT_PROJECTION.json').read_text())['expected']['instructions'],json.loads((O/n/'INPUT_CONTRACT_PROJECTION.json').read_text())['expected']['CTA']]for n,d in D.items()]),'', 'Both are one-kernel stream-0 replays, not the 145,666,048-instruction/two-kernel matrix-vector contract. Current strict proof, frozen full-body qualification and a fresh bounded 4096-byte trace header agree. The preserved whole-body SHA qualification establishes all declared CTAs/warps with terminal EXIT within this trace scope; it does not certify native numerical correctness or capture-time ELF identity.','', '## Performance','',table(['Program','CH-P0','CH-F128','DH-P0','DH-F128','S_CH','S_DH','CH/DH at F128','I = S_DH/S_CH'],[[n,*[next(r['cycles']for r in d['four_closed_sources']if(r['cell'],r['profile'])==p)for p in[('CH','P0'),('CH','F128'),('DH','P0'),('DH','F128')]],d['matched_performance']['S_CH'],d['matched_performance']['S_DH'],d['matched_performance']['R_F128'],d['matched_performance']['I']]for n,d in D.items()]),'', 'P0->F128 changes only `-gpgpu_frfcfs_dram_sched_queue_size` 64->128 within each design. DRAM remains 850 MHz and the L2 cache remains `S:128:128:16,L:B:m:L:L,A:192:4,32:0,32` (10 MiB). The fixed Core shared-credit formula also changes each memory partition shared-credit limit 255->319; this is FR-FCFS-window plus credit expansion, not an isolated queue-capacity intervention. No cross-design capacity/Tag/PIB/finite-service equality is asserted.','', '## Additive counters at the single completed-kernel print boundary','', 'L2 GLOBAL accepted reads and misses use 32-byte sectors. Accepted excludes reservation failures; GLOBAL misses = MISS + SECTOR_MISS. DRAM reads/writes are issued 32-byte data atoms across all20 controllers. All-L2 misses include access types beyond GLOBAL reads; keep these populations separate. Counters below are explicit cumulative values from the one-kernel stream-0 replay, not sums of cumulative snapshots. Retry/admission event counts are not occupancy, duration or critical-path fractions.','']
keys=[('L2_GLOBAL_read_accepted_sectors','L2 GLOBAL accepted read sectors'),('L2_GLOBAL_read_miss_sectors','L2 GLOBAL read miss sectors'),('L2_total_cache_misses','All-L2 miss sectors'),('DRAM_issued_read_atoms32B','DRAM issued read atoms32B'),('DRAM_issued_write_atoms32B','DRAM issued write atoms32B'),('L2_total_cache_pending_hits','All-L2 pending hits'),('L2_total_cache_reservation_fails','All-L2 reservation retry events'),('gpu_stall_dramfull','ICNT->memory blocked-admission events')]
