text+=['## GEMM: facts and limited interpretation','', 'All four closed sources explicitly report zero `n_req`, `n_act`, `n_pre`, `n_rd`, `n_rd_L2_A`, `n_write`, and `n_wr_bk` on every one of20 controllers. L2 GLOBAL read misses, all-L2 misses and L2 reservation failures are also zero. L2 GLOBAL read buckets are all HIT for the measured accepted requests. CH has4,796,228 accepted read sectors; DH1,716,504. Both designs retain exactly the same cycles, selected additive counters, L2 buckets and positive-only retry reasons when F128 is applied.','', 'This excludes exercised DRAM request-window pressure for this fixed sampled condition. It does not show a compute-bound workload: CH still records226,209,642 ordinary-L1 MSHR merge-limit retry events and25,214,976 common Tag-bank conflict attempts; DH records1,165,837 ICNT->memory admission-block events,3,817,106 OO pending-line hits and389,331 ready-but-writeback-blocked events. The misleading legacy name `gpu_stall_dramfull` is an ICNT admission counter and can be nonzero even when issued DRAM traffic is zero. These are observable event populations, not proof of the dominant stall path.','', 'DH finite-service samples52,869,696 and PIB integral3,116,491,485 are identical across F; so are the completion/collection/writeback measures. The speed difference between CH and DH is real for this input/configuration, but causality and hardware cost require the separate frontend architectures and finite service to remain disclosed.','', '## 2DCONV: facts, associations and hypotheses','', 'Facts: CH remains1,548,909 cycles with identical selected cumulative counters, L2 buckets and retry reasons. DH drops462,740->437,573 cycles (25,167 fewer). Both DH runs issue exactly2,097,152 DRAM read atoms (64 MiB); writes increase1,931,720->1,931,952 atoms (+232, +0.0120%). GLOBAL read misses stay2,097,152 and all-L2 misses stay4,193,280. Therefore fewer DRAM reads or fewer miss sectors do not explain this gain. The printed issued-write counts do not certify all dirty cache state has been drained after the measured kernel.','', 'Associations: DH L2 reservation retries fall37.75% (2,546,098->1,584,855) and ICNT admission blocks fall25.00% (3,701,660->2,776,419). Read MISS_QUEUE_FULL drops908,998->165,099; read MSHR merge-limit failures drop1,623,233->1,386,988. Read MSHR entry-capacity failures instead rise82->30,449. OO lower requests rise1,918,754->1,919,808 (+0.05493%); the L2 GLOBAL accepted-sector count is exactly4 times the128-byte OO lower creations in each run. This is a same-design request conservation check, not proof every DRAM request or lower request has a one-to-one critical-path role.','', 'CH has0 ICNT admission-block events and only54 L2 reservation failures, yet315,294,062 ordinary-L1 merge-limit retries and15,720,960 common Tag-bank conflict attempts. DH has a much larger lower-interface retry population. This contrast supports testing whether the coupled downstream expansion changes admission/overlap for DH while CH exposes a different frontend limitation. It does not prove CH is limited exclusively by merge capacity, nor that increasing it would improve performance.','', 'Hypothesis only: FR-FCFS-window/shared-credit expansion changes the timing of lower responses and overlapping requests, reducing some lower admission/retry pressure in DH. Existing event counts and aggregate cycles are consistent with this but do not isolate queue occupancy, queue residence, critical memory dependencies, bank scheduling or credit occupancy. Static nine-tap reuse and increased OO pending hits do not establish a causal cache-hit/MSHR-merge mechanism.','', 'Contrary evidence against a blanket "all service latency improved" claim: DH ready-to-complete sum71,495,415->74,948,733; ready-to-collect sum60,291,527->63,525,333; writeback wait2,199,467->2,341,112. The finite-service retired denominator remains4,716,288. Mean PIB occupancy across64SM samples stays close to saturation; a shorter total runtime does not imply all entry lifetimes shrink.','', '## Typed frontend and finite-service domains','', 'CH PAPER_BASE uses the active common PIB256; DH PAPER_OO uses its OO PIB128. DH generic PIB parameter8 is inactive for OO admission. CH common Tag/PIB fields are never inserted into DH OO-named fields. Unprinted OO PIB-full/Tag-conflict events stay null. CH finite-service extension is disabled; this does not imply its ordinary cache has unlimited service.','']
